From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] fitz: Put the box of a vertical character around its
 vertical origin.

The structured text device started the box of a vertical character one
advance above the glyph origin, which is at the baseline of the glyph,
and let it begin at the glyph origin across the column. A PDF places a
vertical glyph by its vertical origin, the point its advance starts
from, which by default (DW2) lies 880/1000 of the size above and half
the glyph width right of the glyph origin. So the boxes of a vertical
column sat 0.12 em above the glyphs, and a glyph narrower or wider than
one em (a digit or a Latin letter) got a box shifted sideways from the
column, which split the highlight of a column into several quads. The
box is now one em wide, centred across on the vertical origin, starts
at it and ends one advance further on. On the vertical text of the
pdf.js test files the middle of the box is now within 0.02 em of the
middle of the ink (median) both along and across the column, the
highlight of a column is a single quad, and Latin letters set upright
are no longer 0.16 em off. The glyph width comes from the width table
of the PDF font. The device does not know the vertical metrics of a
font, so a font with its own (W2, or another DW2) still gets the
default. Horizontal text is unchanged.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-20.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/fitz/stext-device.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/fitz/stext-device.c b/source/fitz/stext-device.c
index 124676b..7507286 100644
--- a/source/fitz/stext-device.c
+++ b/source/fitz/stext-device.c
@@ -87,6 +87,7 @@ void fz_add_layout_char(fz_context *ctx, fz_layout_block *block, float x, float
 #define SPACE_MAX_DIST 0.8f
 #define BASE_MAX_DIST 0.8f
 #define FAKE_BOLD_MAX_DIST 0.1f
+#define VERTICAL_ORIGIN 0.88f
 
 /* We keep a stack of the different metatexts that apply at any
  * given point (normally none!). Whenever we get some content
@@ -764,6 +765,16 @@ plausible_bullet(int c)
 		0);
 }
 
+static float
+vertical_glyph_width(fz_context *ctx, fz_font *font, int glyph)
+{
+	if (glyph < 0)
+		return 1;
+	if (font->width_table)
+		return (glyph < font->width_count ? font->width_table[glyph] : font->width_default) / 1000.0f;
+	return fz_advance_glyph(ctx, font, glyph, 0);
+}
+
 static void
 fz_add_stext_char_imp(fz_context *ctx, fz_stext_device *dev, fz_font *font, int c, int glyph, fz_matrix trm, float adv, int wmode, int bidi, int force_new_line, int flags)
 {
@@ -812,7 +823,10 @@ fz_add_stext_char_imp(fz_context *ctx, fz_stext_device *dev, fz_font *font, int
 	 *   + p is bottom left.
 	 *   + q is the bottom right
 	 * In vertical mode:
-	 *   + p is top left (where it advanced from)
+	 *   + p is top left (where it advanced from) of a box one em
+	 *     wide around the vertical origin, which a PDF puts half the
+	 *     glyph width right of and 880/1000 of the size above the
+	 *     glyph origin unless the font says otherwise (DW2, W2)
 	 *   + q is bottom left
 	 */
 	if (wmode == 0)
@@ -824,10 +838,11 @@ fz_add_stext_char_imp(fz_context *ctx, fz_stext_device *dev, fz_font *font, int
 	}
 	else
 	{
-		p.x = trm.e - adv * dir.x;
-		p.y = trm.f - adv * dir.y;
-		q.x = trm.e;
-		q.y = trm.f;
+		float across = (vertical_glyph_width(ctx, font, glyph) - 1) / 2;
+		p.x = trm.e + across * trm.a - VERTICAL_ORIGIN * dir.x;
+		p.y = trm.f + across * trm.b - VERTICAL_ORIGIN * dir.y;
+		q.x = p.x + adv * dir.x;
+		q.y = p.y + adv * dir.y;
 	}
 
 	//printf("%g,%g \"%c\" %g,%g\n", p.x, p.y, c, q.x, q.y);
